  <main_text>
    <l n="1">tum. Imaginem vide. Nec ab-</l>
    <l n="2">surda aut vero nimis extranea sen-</l>
    <l n="3">tentia est: cùm &amp; Patibulum re-</l>
    <l n="4">periam singularem ejusmodi re-</l>
    <l n="5">ctumque stipitem dictum. No-</l>
    <l n="6">nius ex Titinio citat:</l>
    <l n="7">— <i>si quisquam hodie *</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>praeter hanc</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Posticum nostrum pepulerit, pa-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>tibulo hoc</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Ei caput defringam.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12" para="true">Et interpretatur <i>Seram</i>, <i>quâ ostia</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>occluduntur</i>, <i>quò hac remotâ val-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>va pateant</i>. Credo eum ex ipso</l>
    <l n="15">argumento fabulæ sic proferre, &amp;</l>
    <l n="16">quòd janitor aliquis atque ostii</l>
    <l n="17">custos hæc dicat. Certè quidem</l>
    <l n="18">Sera est lignum transversum</l>
    <l n="19">quod ostiis opponi solet, in po-</l>
    <l n="20">stem utrimque immissum. Ho-</l>
    <l n="21">die quoque usus. Itaque Glossæ:</l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Sera, μοχλὸς θύρας.</i> Et Poëta</l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>aliquis — excute poste seram.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">Atque</l>
    <l n="25" type="foot" para="true">¹ Ovid. in Amor.</l>
